course: dictionary
lesson: 14488
title: Paved
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Paved means covered with a hard, flat surface, such as stones, bricks or asphalt, so people can walk or drive on it. «The path through the park is paved.» You can tell it is paved because it is flat and hard, not muddy grass.
explain: Pave is a verb, so the word changes like other verbs: pave, paves, paved, paving. «The workers will pave the car park next week.» In this sentence, pave means to cover the ground with a hard surface.
explain: Paved also has a second meaning in the phrase «pave the way». To pave the way for something is to make it easier for it to happen later. «Her hard practice paved the way for her win.» The practice did not cover anything. Ask yourself: what happens later in the sentence? That is your clue.
fact: Paved means covered with a hard, flat surface, such as stones, bricks or asphalt.
fact: «Paved» can describe a thing: «a paved road» or «a paved yard».
fact: «Paved» is also the past form of the verb «pave»: «They paved the road last year.»
fact: «Pave the way» means to make it easier for something to happen later.
fact: «Paving stones» are flat stones used to make a paved surface.
exercise: «The old yard was paved with grey stones.» What was the yard covered with? | Tall trees | *Hard, flat stones | Wet leaves | Soft sand
exercise: Which phrase means to make it easier for something to happen later? | Paint the wall | Pave the sea | *Pave the way | Walk the dog
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that tells you the road is hard and flat: «The Romans built long, paved roads across their empire.» | Romans | long | *paved | across
test: «The children rode their bikes on the paved playground.» Where did they ride? | *On a hard, flat surface | In a muddy field | In the sea | Under a bridge
test: «Her hard work paved the way for her success.» What does paved the way mean here? | It covered a road with stones | It ended her success | It made the work harder | *It made her success easier to happen
exam: «The council will pave the old path so buses can drive on it safely.» What does pave mean here? | To dig a deep hole | To cut down the trees | *To cover with a hard, flat surface | To paint a sign on the wall
